IMPORT prelude

-- South Australian concessions switched on by a Commonwealth card or payment -- shared nouns for the seat-neutral core
-- (colc-concessions.l4, colc-levy.l4, colc-vehicles.l4) and the concession holder's seat (colc-seat.l4).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, taken from the Open Australian Legal
-- Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text is as at the corpus scrape and may be out of date. See NOTES.md and SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- Conventions. A financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June and is named here by the calendar year in which it BEGINS:
-- 2024 is the 2024/2025 financial year. Money is in Australian dollars. A share of land is a fraction from 0 to 1.
-- Dates are DATE values; comparisons go through DATE_SERIAL (the stable l4 has no DATE comparison without daydate).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Shared nouns -- South Australian concessions for Commonwealth card and payment holders`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, reg 3(3): an indexed amount is "rounded up to the nearest multiple of
-- 10 cents".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to the nearest 10 cents` `amount` MEANS
    CEILING (`amount` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 10

§§ `Days`

-- The stable prelude has no YMD; this shim gives one.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` `is on or before` `other` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` `is before` `other` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

-- The number of days from one day to a later one (0 for the same day).
GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `first` `to` `last` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `last` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `first`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS 1)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first of the month after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12
    THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1) 1 1
    ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS 1) 1

-- "a period of one month after" a day (Motor Vehicles Act 1959, s 38A(3)). READING: the same day of the next month, or
-- the last day of the next month where it is shorter (one month after 31 January is 28 or 29 February). The Act does
-- not say; the Acts Interpretation Act 1915 (SA) is not deposited.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`one month after` `the day` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `next month`) (DATE_MONTH `next month`) (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` `days in next month`)
    WHERE
        `next month` MEANS `the first of the month after` `the day`
        `days in next month` MEANS `days from` `next month` `to` (`the first of the month after` `next month`)

-- The number of complete calendar months from `first` (counted from the start of that day) to `end` (counted to the
-- start of that day): from 15 March to 15 June is 3; from 15 March to 14 June is 2.
GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`complete months from` `first` `to the start of` `end` MEANS
    IF `raw months` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `raw months`
    WHERE
        `month count` MEANS
            ((DATE_YEAR `end` MINUS DATE_YEAR `first`) TIMES 12)
            PLUS (DATE_MONTH `end` MINUS DATE_MONTH `first`)
        `raw months` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `end` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `first`
            THEN `month count` MINUS 1
            ELSE `month count`

§§ `The financial year`

GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`1 July of the financial year beginning in` `the year it begins` MEANS
    YMD `the year it begins` 7 1

§§ `Commonwealth cards and payments`

-- The Commonwealth cards and payments that the South Australian texts name. Holding the card or receiving the payment
-- is a FACT (borrowed Commonwealth terms: Social Security Act 1991, Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986, Military
-- Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004, Farm Household Support Act 2014). Each text picks its own list from these:
-- Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, reg 3(1) ("prescribed card", "prescribed payments") and reg 6(b);
-- Emergency Services Funding (Remissions--Land) Regulations 2014, reg 6(5). Where the two texts name different
-- programs (the Community Development programs), each name is its own choice; where they use two names for what reads
-- as one program (Self-Employment Assistance), one choice serves both (finding 10).
DECLARE `Commonwealth card or payment` IS ONE OF
    `a Pensioner Concession Card`
    `a Low Income Health Care Card`
    `a TPI Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    `a War Widows Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    `a Gold Repatriation Health Card (EDA)`
    `a Gold Repatriation Health Card issued for 80 or more impairment points under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`
    `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card`
    `an Austudy payment`
    `a JobSeeker payment`
    `a parenting payment`
    `a special benefit`
    `a youth allowance`
    `an Abstudy payment`
    `payments under the Community Development Employment Project or the Remote Jobs and Economic Development Program`
    `payments under the Community Development Program`
    `Self-Employment Assistance allowance payments`
    `a war widow's pension under the law of the United Kingdom or New Zealand`
    `farm household allowance payments under the Farm Household Support Act 2014`
    `none of these`
